OmacVM Cocoa: the window's spare present surfaces volatile while it is out of sight

What: after 2 s out of sight (macOS's occlusion state: minimised, covered,
another Space, the screen locked, closed with Keep running) every present
IOSurface that Core Animation does not show or read (in use, or the
layer's contents) gets IOSurfaceSetPurgeable volatile. In sight again, the
surfaces come back non-volatile before the frame; a surface taken for a
frame comes back first; one that macOS emptied meanwhile is drawn whole
(the partial present's state for every surface set to full). QEMU's thread
looks at every refresh tick (500 ms while out of sight) and present. A
refusal from macOS logs once and stops the rule for the run.
OMACVM_PRESENT_VOLATILE=0 keeps every surface, as before;
OMACVM_PRESENT_HIDDEN (frames drawn out of sight) keeps them too. qemu.log:
"cocoa: present surfaces: spare ones volatile while the window is out of
sight" (or "all kept (...)") once, and at each return after one went
volatile "cocoa: present: in sight again: N spare surfaces were volatile,
M emptied by macOS (drawn whole)" and "cocoa: present: first frame N ms
after the window was seen again". Test hooks: OMACVM_TEST_PRESENT_PURGE=1
empties each surface for real (kIOSurfacePurgeableEmpty) before it comes
back; OMACVM_TEST_SIGHT=FILE (test mode only) takes the window's sight
from the file ("seen" / "unseen", read every 0.25 s) instead of macOS's
occlusion notices, as a locked test Mac shows no window as seen.
Why: out of sight QEMU draws nothing, yet kept 5 surfaces: 310 MiB of its
footprint at 5120x2880 8-bit or lossless, 592 MiB in half float. With
this, 4 of 5 at 5K: -225 MiB (8-bit, lossless), -450 MiB (half float),
by the per-surface host costs in the logic patch. Host test of a real
purge (Mac mini M4, macOS 27.0, plain and lossless 5K surfaces bound as
GL textures): Empty then non-volatile reports Empty, the old picture is
gone, a new draw into it shows and the footprint comes back.
Upstream: OmacVM's own. Needs omacvm-cocoa-present-volatile-logic.patch.
Tests: Tests/display/test-present-volatile.sh <patched ui/cocoa.m> (the
wiring; --self-test: every check fails on the code before); VM rows in
the PR (a real window on a locked Mac: footprint seen, unseen 10 s, seen;
check mode and the purge hook).
